      "seed": 1864168741,
      "version": 164,
      "versionNonce": 1975553291,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783722061188,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Part 1: How WebSockets are Implemented",
      "fontSize": 29.457602786578345,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Part 1: How WebSockets are Implemented",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "nifRYGSLPYG0_uYjTNA3i",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2929.005646155175,
      "y": -3500.224929055329,
      "width": 978.1095489170831,
      "height": 73.64400696644584,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2I",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1429478315,
      "version": 164,
      "versionNonce": 1608561579,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783722061188,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Standard Protocol: WebSockets are defined by standard IETF RFC\nspecifications.",
      "fontSize": 29.457602786578345,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Standard Protocol: WebSockets are defined by standard IETF RFC specifications.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Xim1RyxmgWKcmWmxzrD5c",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -3028.9994104921384,
      "y": -3430.263122437206,
      "width": 1178.09707759101,
      "height": 110.46601044966879,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2J",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1550649477,
      "version": 164,
      "versionNonce": 1820526155,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783722061188,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Libraries: Just as we use Express or Hono to build HTTP servers, we use existing\nlibraries (like ws in Node.js) to build WebSocket servers rather than implementing\nthe protocol from scratch.",
      "fontSize": 29.457602786578345,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Libraries: Just as we use Express or Hono to build HTTP servers, we use existing libraries (like ws in Node.js) to build WebSocket servers rather than implementing the protocol from scratch.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "aFqL-mOBhYw8pjpKS6S8P",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -3022.857525482428,
      "y": -3305.0683105942476,
      "width": 1165.8133075715898,
      "height": 110.46601044966879,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2K",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 858353227,
      "version": 164,
      "versionNonce": 1652688107,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783722061188,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Low-Level Custom Code: High-performance trading firms (like Jane Street)\nsometimes build WebSocket servers from scratch in C++ or Rust to achieve ultra-\nlow latency.",
      "fontSize": 29.457602786578345,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Low-Level Custom Code: High-performance trading firms (like Jane Street) sometimes build WebSocket servers from scratch in C++ or Rust to achieve ultra-low latency.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "aNnBKZr1rQxcD5Suh3xyo",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2706.875290884278,
      "y": -3121.189007475098,
      "width": 557.2491069299766,
      "height": 36.82200348322292,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2L",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 19116005,
      "version": 168,
      "versionNonce": 1231564683,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783722061188,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Part 2: Socket.io vs. Pure WebSockets",
      "fontSize": 29.45760278657835,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Part 2: Socket.io vs. Pure WebSockets",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "QEvXX7juIU2FRtgSpfGkX",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2974.070235135744,
      "y": -3088.049204340198,
      "width": 1091.6389954329086,
      "height": 73.64400696644584,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2M",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1478192363,
      "version": 180,
      "versionNonce": 1399850539,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783722061188,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Socket.io is a beginner-friendly library for persistent communication, but the\ninstructor recommends avoiding it for serious projects.",
      "fontSize": 29.457602786578345,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Socket.io is a beginner-friendly library for persistent communication, but the instructor recommends avoiding it for serious projects.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Jso9Vz4y95J9AT4uc8ott",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -3000.140321478829,
      "y": -2999.6763959804625,
      "width": 1143.779168119079,
      "height": 73.64400696644584,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2N",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1531865925,
      "version": 180,
      "versionNonce": 126093515,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783722061188,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The Issue with Socket.io: It is a proprietary layer built on top of WebSockets.\nIf you use it on the backend, you must use a Socket.io client on the frontend.",
      "fontSize": 29.457602786578345,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The Issue with Socket.io: It is a proprietary layer built on top of WebSockets. If you use it on the backend, you must use a Socket.io client on the frontend.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "yW48A8RGDxNGSaW5r9lnB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2990.993613553038,
      "y": -2929.714589362339,
      "width": 1125.485752267497,
      "height": 110.46601044966879,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2O",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 395614091,
      "version": 180,
      "versionNonce": 725530475,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783722061188,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Cross-Platform Limitations: If you build a mobile app in Android or a service in\nRust, finding and maintaining Socket.io client libraries for those ecosystems is\ndifficult.",
      "fontSize": 29.457602786578345,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Cross-Platform Limitations: If you build a mobile app in Android or a service in Rust, finding and maintaining Socket.io client libraries for those ecosystems is difficult.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ZlHXW1bVvkKPuCMY9_ldR",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2994.4990754764385,
      "y": -2786.1087757777696,
      "width": 1132.4966761142978,
      "height": 73.64400696644584,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2P",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1263188645,
      "version": 180,
      "versionNonce": 1827312139,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783722061188,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "WebSockets Benefit: WebSockets are standard and natively supported out-of-\nthe-box by web browsers (new WebSocket(...)), Android, iOS, Rust, Go, etc.",
      "fontSize": 29.457602786578345,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "WebSockets Benefit: WebSockets are standard and natively supported out-of-the-box by web browsers (new WebSocket(...)), Android, iOS, Rust, Go, etc.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Rp1E6HP8r-ZOTu_7MXKxP",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2987.4094462787525,
      "y": -3796.0597587150623,
      "width": 1149.48046875,
      "height": 87.3677059076391,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2Q",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 81850629,
      "version": 89,
      "versionNonce": 256790098,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784661081997,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Websockets basics and socket io ",
      "fontSize": 69.89416472611128,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Websockets basics and socket io ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "9ChMmAHV9S9--xYl48xZs",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1672.3076521588198,
      "y": -3537.839467446007,
      "width": 1063.0764283876558,
      "height": 652.0676506580463,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2R",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1102618830,
      "version": 233,
      "versionNonce": 1405061609,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784711867328,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "WebSockets & Serverless (Cloudflare Workers): Serverless\narchitectures are bad for WebSockets because serverless\nfunctions spin up and shut down quickly, whereas WebSockets\nrequire long-lived, persistent TCP connections.\nSystem Failures:\nIf an auxiliary service (like notifications or queues) is down,\nyour main app can still function (e.g., balance updates succeed,\nbut notifications fail).\nIf the primary backend is down, your app experiences complete\ndowntime.\nDatabase Optimization for Real-Time Apps: Avoid hitting the\ndatabase on every single incoming WebSocket message (e.g.,\nchat apps). Instead, buffer messages in a queue and perform\nbatch inserts to reduce DB load.\n",
      "fontSize": 34.776941368429135,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "WebSockets & Serverless (Cloudflare Workers): Serverless architectures are bad for WebSockets because serverless functions spin up and shut down quickly, whereas WebSockets require long-lived, persistent TCP connections.\nSystem Failures:\nIf an auxiliary service (like notifications or queues) is down, your main app can still function (e.g., balance updates succeed, but notifications fail).\nIf the primary backend is down, your app experiences complete downtime.\nDatabase Optimization for Real-Time Apps: Avoid hitting the database on every single incoming WebSocket message (e.g., chat apps). Instead, buffer messages in a queue and perform batch inserts to reduce DB load.\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
